xnu 0272: the canvas scale in 16-byte lanes

The 32/25 block was already spelled out, but it still cost a scalar load per
output pixel: 32 loads and 8 stores per 32 pixels, 4-5 ms a swap (ring240), and
the frames that arrive just past their vsync are what a drag feels as steps.

Each group of four outputs reads four consecutive source bytes at a constant
offset inside the 25-pixel (100-byte) block, so one 16-byte load per group and
one byte shuffle is the whole job: 8 loads, 6 shuffles and 8 stores per block,
and clang lowers each shuffle to a single `tbl`. The pattern is the same
floor(i * 25 / 32) the scalar version spelled out.

